# Test: the RFC 2661 control bytes ze EMITS, checked by an oracle outside ze.
#
# VALIDATES: every assertion here reads a byte off a real UDP datagram with a
#            native Go fixture parser that shares no code with ze, and compares it against a
#            value computed here from the RFC text.
# PREVENTS:  producer and verifier agreeing with each other and with no other
#            implementation -- the defect shape that shipped five times on
#            2026-08-01 in the IKE stack (bare OID vs AlgorithmIdentifier
#            SEQUENCE, a one-octet OpCode read as four, an MSK nobody else
#            computes). Every one of those was unit-green for months.
#
# Why unit evidence cannot reach these obligations:
#   - the AVP/header shape is asserted in Go against ze's OWN AVP iterator
#     (internal/component/l2tp/avp.go -- NewAVPIterator), so an encoder and a
#     decoder that share a misreading agree;
#   - the tunnel-auth digest is asserted against ze's OWN helper
#     (internal/component/l2tp/auth.go -- VerifyChallengeResponse CALLS
#     ChallengeResponse), so the two can never disagree by construction.
#
# Every check is POSITIVE: it names a byte that must be present and equal to an
# externally computed value. Nothing passes because something failed to happen
# (ai/rules/interop-and-goal-validation.md, vacuity traps).
#
# RFC requirement: RFC2661-4.1-2 positive -- the Message Type AVP (type 0) is the
# FIRST AVP in the SCCRP ze puts on the wire, read off the datagram by an
# external parser rather than by ze's own AVP iterator.
# RFC requirement: RFC2661-x-1 positive -- reserved bits 8-11 of the L2TP control
# header ze emits are zero on the wire.
# RFC requirement: RFC2661-4.1-1 positive -- every AVP ze emits carries reserved
# bits 2-5 clear.


stdin=config:terminator=EOF_CONF
l2tp {
	enabled true
	shared-secret s3cr3t
}
environment {
	l2tp {
		server main {
			ip 127.0.0.1
			port $PORT
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

option=env:var=ze.log.l2tp:value=debug
option=env:var=ze.l2tp.skip-kernel-probe:value=true

cmd=background:seq=1:exec=ze -:stdin=config
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze-test fixture l2tp/rfc2661-emitted-control-shape $PORT:timeout=20s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=OK: all RFC 2661 emitted-shape checks passed
# The daemon's own confirmation that the independently computed SCCCN response
# verified. A positive signal, so the acceptance step cannot pass vacuously.
expect=stderr:contains=tunnel now established
